WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.824 --> 00:00:04.657
Neil Laughton: OK, ride towards...

00:00:04.657 --> 00:00:06.350
Caroline Aghajanian: Oh, my
God, oh, my God, oh, my God, ah!

00:00:06.350 --> 00:00:08.400
On this episode of "Travel Dares,"

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:10.890
Nico and I are going to learn how to ride

00:00:10.890 --> 00:00:12.880
penny-farthing bicycles.

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:16.100
Neil: Push, push, push, hop up, up.

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:18.270
Nico Reyes: And I'm taking
Caroline to Cambridge University,

00:00:18.270 --> 00:00:20.170
where we're gonna learn how to punt.

00:00:20.170 --> 00:00:24.510
Caroline: I was born to
turn this punt around.

00:00:24.510 --> 00:00:26.170
Come join us on our adventures

00:00:26.170 --> 00:00:28.483
on this episode of "Travel Dares."

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:34.340
This is "Travel Dares,"

00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:37.250
the show where we do daring
activities all over Europe,

00:00:37.250 --> 00:00:39.750
empowered by my Marriott
Bonvoy Boundless card.

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:42.570
Nico: London is one of the most
popular travel destinations

00:00:42.570 --> 00:00:44.350
in the entire world.

00:00:44.350 --> 00:00:46.280
But, today, we're gonna be doing two dares

00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:48.230
that are a bit more off the beaten path.

00:00:48.230 --> 00:00:50.500
Caroline: Nico, you're going first.

00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:51.875
Nico: Let's see this clue.

00:00:54.270 --> 00:00:57.220
These clues are just
getting more and more vague.

00:00:57.220 --> 00:01:01.194
My mind is going to, like, making candles

00:01:01.194 --> 00:01:03.360
or churning butter or something.

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:06.080
Maybe we're making clocks,
we're turning back time.

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:07.320
Caroline: Penny-farthing bicycles

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:10.180
were invented in England
in the 19th century.

00:01:10.180 --> 00:01:11.470
London's penny-farthing club

00:01:11.470 --> 00:01:14.500
lets you see the city on
these huge antique bikes.

00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:17.100
So close, so close, OK,

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:19.890
all right, now you stand right here.

00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:22.920
OK, Nico, take your blindfold off,

00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:26.050
because we're riding
penny-farthing bicycles

00:01:26.050 --> 00:01:27.218
all around town.

00:01:27.218 --> 00:01:30.510
Nico: [laughs] Wait, these old bicycles?

00:01:30.510 --> 00:01:32.700
I've never seen one of these in person.

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:34.700
It's huge.
Caroline: Yeah, it is.

00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:42.880
Neil: So, the penny-farthing bicycle,

00:01:42.880 --> 00:01:44.870
actually called an ordinary bicycle,

00:01:44.870 --> 00:01:48.200
was invented in 1869
and became quite popular

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:49.440
in Central London.

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:51.530
Everyone loves to see us ride the bikes,

00:01:51.530 --> 00:01:53.460
and at 8 foot tall, up in the air,

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:56.140
you get a really fantastic
view of all the great sights.

00:01:56.140 --> 00:01:58.670
The penny-farthing bike tour's
a three-hour experience.

00:01:58.670 --> 00:02:00.220
The first half of the experience

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:02.010
is learning to safely and competently,

00:02:02.010 --> 00:02:03.800
confidently, ride the bicycle,

00:02:03.800 --> 00:02:06.760
and then we go on a guided
tour of Central London,

00:02:06.760 --> 00:02:08.910
seeing all the great
sights of Westminster.

00:02:10.420 --> 00:02:11.870
What I'll do is I'll demonstrate first.

00:02:11.870 --> 00:02:12.703
Nico: OK.

00:02:12.703 --> 00:02:13.536
Neil: And then it'll be your turn.

00:02:13.536 --> 00:02:14.390
Nico: Oh, gosh.

00:02:14.390 --> 00:02:15.223
Caroline: Is there, like,

00:02:15.223 --> 00:02:18.031
training wheels we can put on the bike?

00:02:18.031 --> 00:02:18.980
Neil: Certainly not.

00:02:18.980 --> 00:02:21.310
So, this is how it looks in real life.

00:02:21.310 --> 00:02:24.117
Push, push, push, hop up, up.

00:02:25.212 --> 00:02:26.045
Caroline: I can't do that.

00:02:26.045 --> 00:02:27.730
Nico: Oh, no, you make it look so easy.

00:02:27.730 --> 00:02:28.720
Caroline: I can't do...I'm sweating.

00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:30.470
Neil: OK, I turn the corner,

00:02:30.470 --> 00:02:32.250
straight line, I wanna get off,

00:02:32.250 --> 00:02:34.120
come down the peg

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:35.442
and hop off like so, thank you.

00:02:35.442 --> 00:02:37.368
Caroline: Oh, my gosh.

00:02:37.368 --> 00:02:40.520
[Nico and Caroline clapping]

00:02:40.520 --> 00:02:43.460
Neil: Slide onto the
seat, nice and relaxed.

00:02:43.460 --> 00:02:44.293
Nico: Yup.

00:02:44.293 --> 00:02:46.030
Neil: And you're in charge of steering.

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:49.787
Nico: Oh, no, I'm trying
not to freak out right now.

00:02:49.787 --> 00:02:51.170
Neil: No, no relax, you're doing it,

00:02:51.170 --> 00:02:52.338
you're doing it.
Caroline: You got this, Nico.

00:02:52.338 --> 00:02:53.388
Nico: I'm doing good.
Neil: You're riding

00:02:53.388 --> 00:02:54.868
a penny-farthing all by yourself.

00:02:54.868 --> 00:02:57.223
Get off, and then dismount.

00:02:58.070 --> 00:03:00.592
Stand up on the next peg, just relax.

00:03:00.592 --> 00:03:01.766
Caroline: I'm a little short.

00:03:01.766 --> 00:03:03.491
My feet keep slipping on the pedals.

00:03:04.594 --> 00:03:05.800
Neil: No.
Caroline: Oh, God.

00:03:05.800 --> 00:03:07.004
Neil: Well done.

00:03:07.004 --> 00:03:08.820
[Nico laughs]

00:03:08.820 --> 00:03:09.653
Let's go.

00:03:09.653 --> 00:03:11.794
Nico: [groans] My heart was pounding.

00:03:11.794 --> 00:03:13.753
I thought I was a goner.

00:03:17.558 --> 00:03:19.145
Neil: OK, toe.
Nico: Handlebars.

00:03:19.145 --> 00:03:22.280
Neil: Toe, stand up, next
peg, slight, that's it.

00:03:22.280 --> 00:03:24.060
Caroline: She's so good.

00:03:24.060 --> 00:03:24.974
Neil: OK, ride towards...

00:03:24.974 --> 00:03:25.807
Caroline: Oh, my God, oh,
my God, oh, my God, aah!

00:03:25.807 --> 00:03:27.200
Neil: Ride towards me.

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:29.040
Nico: Caroline, you're doing it!

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:30.027
Neil: That's it!

00:03:30.027 --> 00:03:31.270
Caroline: But we didn't fall.

00:03:31.270 --> 00:03:32.245
Nico: Yeah.
Caroline: We didn't fall.

00:03:32.245 --> 00:03:33.220
Nico: We haven't fallen at all.

00:03:33.220 --> 00:03:34.053
Neil: OK. Congratulations,

00:03:34.053 --> 00:03:35.444
you're both penny-farthing riders.

00:03:35.444 --> 00:03:37.890
Caroline: Time to put
our training to the test.

00:03:37.890 --> 00:03:39.340
Nico: Let's get the wheels rolling.

00:03:39.340 --> 00:03:40.700
Caroline: Whoo!

00:03:40.700 --> 00:03:41.533
Hey!

00:03:42.940 --> 00:03:44.830
Riding!

00:03:44.830 --> 00:03:47.250
Yay!

00:03:47.250 --> 00:03:49.940
Wow, I think we're really
getting the hang of it.

00:03:49.940 --> 00:03:51.754
Nico: I think so, too.

00:03:51.754 --> 00:03:54.270
Caroline: Out of the way, I can't stop!

00:03:54.270 --> 00:03:57.330
We are free riding down the road.

00:03:57.330 --> 00:03:58.940
Down these English roads.

00:03:58.940 --> 00:04:00.615
Nico: I'm glad we're doing it together.

00:04:00.615 --> 00:04:01.724
Caroline: I know!

00:04:12.581 --> 00:04:14.801
Caroline: We did it! Oh, my gosh!

00:04:14.801 --> 00:04:15.641
Neil: You did so well!

00:04:15.641 --> 00:04:16.537
Well done, excellent!
Caroline: Thanks so much.

00:04:16.537 --> 00:04:17.636
Well done, we did it!

00:04:17.636 --> 00:04:18.469
Caroline: Yes!

00:04:18.469 --> 00:04:19.333
Neil: Penny-farthing riders?

00:04:19.333 --> 00:04:20.166
Caroline: Yes.

00:04:20.166 --> 00:04:20.999
Neil: Let's go!

00:04:20.999 --> 00:04:23.350
Caroline: We did it, yes!
Nico: Whoo, we did it!

00:04:23.350 --> 00:04:24.690
Caroline: Nico, we rode all the way

00:04:24.690 --> 00:04:26.280
to the London Eye without falling!

00:04:26.280 --> 00:04:29.050
Nico: No, we didn't fall at
all! Which is all I wanted.

00:04:29.050 --> 00:04:31.360
Caroline: Yeah. Now
it's time for the clue.

00:04:31.360 --> 00:04:32.193
Nico: There you go.

00:04:32.193 --> 00:04:33.052
Caroline: Ready.

00:04:35.060 --> 00:04:36.710
Oh, my God.
Nico: Give me your thoughts.

00:04:36.710 --> 00:04:40.289
We're going to Hogwarts!
Nico: Give me your thoughts.

00:04:40.289 --> 00:04:41.690
Whoo!

00:04:41.690 --> 00:04:43.470
I'm getting, like, a few things popping

00:04:43.470 --> 00:04:47.580
in my head, like books, school, magic.

00:04:47.580 --> 00:04:48.850
I hope we're not taking a test,

00:04:48.850 --> 00:04:50.590
'cause I'm not a good test-taker.

00:04:50.590 --> 00:04:53.500
Nico: Punting is the No. 1
thing to do here at Cambridge.

00:04:53.500 --> 00:04:56.340
You get to see all of these
amazing sights of the university

00:04:56.340 --> 00:04:59.260
right on the water, and I
can't wait to show Caroline.

00:04:59.260 --> 00:05:00.790
Caroline: I feel like we're
at a farm or something.

00:05:00.790 --> 00:05:03.730
Nico: OK, stop right here.

00:05:03.730 --> 00:05:04.570
Caroline: OK.

00:05:04.570 --> 00:05:06.030
Nico: Take off your blindfold,

00:05:06.030 --> 00:05:08.350
'cause we're at Cambridge University,

00:05:08.350 --> 00:05:11.020
and we're about to go
punting in these boats.

00:05:11.020 --> 00:05:12.519
Caroline: Punting?
Nico: [laughing] Yes.

00:05:12.519 --> 00:05:14.203
Caroline: I've never even heard of that!

00:05:24.300 --> 00:05:25.770
Caroline: I am super stoked.

00:05:25.770 --> 00:05:27.240
I really want to learn how to do this.

00:05:27.240 --> 00:05:28.073
Nico: Ready to go?

00:05:28.073 --> 00:05:29.256
Caroline: Yeah.
Nico: Let's do it!

00:05:29.256 --> 00:05:31.690
I literally can't wait
to sit back and chill

00:05:31.690 --> 00:05:34.300
while Caroline punts
me all over Cambridge.

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:36.058
Caroline: I'm so, like, relaxed already.

00:05:36.058 --> 00:05:37.890
Like, I'm just chilling.

00:05:37.890 --> 00:05:39.170
Fryderyk Lukasik: Well,
punting was originally used

00:05:39.170 --> 00:05:41.040
for transporting goods across the river

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:42.920
from Cambridge to Ely.

00:05:42.920 --> 00:05:45.380
To be a good punter, you
definitely need good sea legs

00:05:45.380 --> 00:05:46.650
and good balance, otherwise you might

00:05:46.650 --> 00:05:47.995
find yourself in the water.

00:05:47.995 --> 00:05:49.661
[Caroline gasps]
Nico: Look at that!

00:05:49.661 --> 00:05:51.140
Caroline: Oh, my God!

00:05:51.140 --> 00:05:52.665
Fryderyk: That's King's
College Chapel right there.

00:05:52.665 --> 00:05:54.680
Caroline: Oh!
Nico: King's College Chapel.

00:05:54.680 --> 00:05:55.870
All right, Caroline, what do you think

00:05:55.870 --> 00:05:57.500
your technique is gonna be?

00:05:57.500 --> 00:05:59.950
Caroline: I'm just gonna try
to keep a lot of pressure

00:05:59.950 --> 00:06:03.510
on my legs, and then trust the...[laughs]

00:06:03.510 --> 00:06:04.343
Nico: Trust the pole!

00:06:04.343 --> 00:06:07.017
Caroline: Trust the pole and,
like, to guide me straight.

00:06:07.880 --> 00:06:08.950
Fryderyk: There you go.

00:06:08.950 --> 00:06:09.783
Caroline: Whoo!

00:06:09.783 --> 00:06:12.070
Fryderyk: You just want
to pick it up like this,

00:06:12.070 --> 00:06:12.903
drop it in, and just push.

00:06:12.903 --> 00:06:14.750
Caroline: OK.
Fryderyk: OK, ready?

00:06:14.750 --> 00:06:16.570
Perfect, perfect, now push.

00:06:16.570 --> 00:06:17.803
Nico: Push, Caroline.

00:06:20.740 --> 00:06:21.880
We moved a little!

00:06:21.880 --> 00:06:23.118
Caroline: Here we go!

00:06:23.118 --> 00:06:24.295
Uh-oh, we are turning,

00:06:24.295 --> 00:06:25.128
I need to steer the other way.

00:06:25.128 --> 00:06:26.520
Fryderyk: So, if you want to go the left.

00:06:26.520 --> 00:06:28.073
Caroline: Oh, this way?
Nico: Left? Go left.

00:06:28.073 --> 00:06:29.681
Caroline: Go left.
Nico: Stake it left.

00:06:29.681 --> 00:06:31.780
Caroline: OK, one, two, and.

00:06:31.780 --> 00:06:33.004
Nico: That might be t...

00:06:33.004 --> 00:06:34.421
[laughing]

00:06:34.421 --> 00:06:35.834
you got it?

00:06:35.834 --> 00:06:37.251
Caroline: Yes!

00:06:38.214 --> 00:06:39.410
Whoo!

00:06:39.410 --> 00:06:40.300
All right, where do you guys

00:06:40.300 --> 00:06:41.393
wanna go in Cambridge?

00:06:41.393 --> 00:06:42.630
Hmm, you wanna go to class?

00:06:42.630 --> 00:06:44.070
Nico: You're taking us for a spin.

00:06:44.070 --> 00:06:47.320
Caroline: Yeah, we're going
for a spin. Buckle up.

00:06:47.320 --> 00:06:50.523
I was born to turn this punt around.

00:06:51.620 --> 00:06:53.923
Guys, I am punting in heels.

00:06:53.923 --> 00:06:56.830
If that doesn't get me an extra star,

00:06:56.830 --> 00:06:58.450
I don't know what will.

00:06:58.450 --> 00:07:01.160
Uh-oh, well, never mind,
I lost, that's really...

00:07:01.160 --> 00:07:02.571
Nico: Oh, we're gonna crash a little.

00:07:02.571 --> 00:07:05.593
Caroline: Oh, my God, aah, oh, no, sorry!

00:07:07.023 --> 00:07:09.292
Sorry, that's my bad. Wow.

00:07:09.292 --> 00:07:10.914
Man: Don't fall off.

00:07:10.914 --> 00:07:12.397
Caroline: I'm trying!

00:07:12.397 --> 00:07:14.030
I think I'm done, Fryderyk.

00:07:14.030 --> 00:07:15.717
I'm gonna give this back to you.

00:07:15.717 --> 00:07:17.439
Nico: Let me save you.

00:07:17.439 --> 00:07:18.286
Caroline, you did it!

00:07:18.286 --> 00:07:19.527
Caroline: I did it!

00:07:27.238 --> 00:07:29.270
Nico, I had such an
amazing time in London,

00:07:29.270 --> 00:07:30.940
it's literally so beautiful,

00:07:30.940 --> 00:07:31.970
especially from the hotel.

00:07:31.970 --> 00:07:33.570
You can see the River Thames,

00:07:33.570 --> 00:07:35.990
the London Eye, it's so amazing.

00:07:35.990 --> 00:07:37.060
Nico: It's a gorgeous view.

00:07:37.060 --> 00:07:40.600
Caroline: Nico, penny-farthing
is not an easy thing to do.

00:07:40.600 --> 00:07:43.490
It takes a bit of skill
to learn everything,

00:07:43.490 --> 00:07:46.300
but you got on, you rode
all the way around town,

00:07:46.300 --> 00:07:48.050
and you didn't fall.

00:07:48.050 --> 00:07:51.810
And for that, you are getting
a five out of five stars.

00:07:51.810 --> 00:07:53.493
Nico: Five stars on this,

00:07:53.493 --> 00:07:55.710
I did not think it was gonna happen.

00:07:55.710 --> 00:07:59.130
I was so scared I was
gonna fall the whole time.

00:07:59.130 --> 00:08:00.320
Caroline.
Caroline: Yes.

00:08:00.320 --> 00:08:02.780
Nico: I'm gonna start off by
saying how much I love you.

00:08:02.780 --> 00:08:03.960
Caroline: Nico!

00:08:03.960 --> 00:08:05.468
Nico: And how much I appreciated

00:08:05.468 --> 00:08:07.520
your enthusiasm and your energy

00:08:07.520 --> 00:08:08.993
when we went out punting.

00:08:09.915 --> 00:08:10.748
But. [laughs]

00:08:10.748 --> 00:08:12.970
Caroline: "But." There has to be a but!

00:08:12.970 --> 00:08:16.560
Nico: But we did spend
more time going in circles

00:08:16.560 --> 00:08:18.890
than we did getting anywhere,

00:08:18.890 --> 00:08:23.290
so I think I'm gonna have to
give you a solid four stars.

00:08:23.290 --> 00:08:24.670
Caroline: OK.
Nico: Solid four.

00:08:24.670 --> 00:08:25.610
Caroline: I will take that.

00:08:25.610 --> 00:08:27.660
Cambridge was absolutely beautiful.

00:08:27.660 --> 00:08:28.493
Nico: It was gorgeous.

00:08:28.493 --> 00:08:30.630
So I didn't really mind
going in circles that much.

00:08:30.630 --> 00:08:32.930
We got 360 views. [laughs]

00:08:32.930 --> 00:08:34.745
Caroline: Nico, we have
just a few more hours

00:08:34.745 --> 00:08:37.070
left in London, so let's hit the town.

00:08:37.070 --> 00:08:37.903
Nico: Cheers!

00:08:37.903 --> 00:08:38.810
Caroline: Cheers!

